{
  "comment": "The Meerkat (the wormhole vessel, 2026-10-27): where each artifact parameter lives in the game. key = the studio's own key, which IS the field's name on MeerkatSolitonConfig (the page's GAME_NAMES); asset + field = the Unity config field it becomes. Lab-only (never in the game): aiTau (the sim's steering response - the game's AI flies with AIPilot), the stand-in hull's lope*. cruise / pitchYaw / roll / bankShare are the prefab's MeerkatVesselTransformer (bankShare x roll = RollScaler, set by author_meerkat_assets.py), not plain fields. Rounds 13-21 (the Omnicrystal's network, MEERKAT.md section 7): omniAtOnce, soil*, the page's labyrinthRing*, labyrinthRibs, labyrinthRoughness and forkHintSeconds are not ported yet. Edit this file, never the assets by hand. Round 23 (Garrett's soliton): areaL0 / areaL10 (the surface area by the hull's Space level, read at use time from its ResourceSystem, so kSpaceLevel is lab-only), suckRadius, suckSpeed, swallowShare, carrySpeed, carryStretch, carryTwist, fireSpeed, fireGlideSeconds (MeerkatSwallow); bounceRestitution is the shared PrismMotionConfig's shieldBounceRestitution (0.6), not a Meerkat field. Round 24: a single tunnel is slid as a network is, so rideEntryMultiplier and rideMidMultiplier are retired. Round 26: carrySpeed retired - a carried prism or crystal moves at the slide's top speed, held behind its tunnel's rider. Garrett's kit (approved by Yash 2026-10-28, R_VesselActions/MEERKAT.md section 10): its plain keys boostOut, sentinelPool, sentinelPoolL5, guardShare, aiZapRate and portalShare map here by the same names; its L0/L10 pairs rushL0/L10, zapPetalsL0/L10 and portalSizeL0/L10 are the ElementalFloat blocks rush, zapPetals and portalSize. 2026-10-29 (Yash: one clear jelly look, no water): the page's look keys are not mapped and their fields are gone - warpStrength, dentStrength, ripple*, bridgeVisibility, bridgeGlass, bridgeWhite, the page's trunk* / branch* / root* look keys, tubeInner and formedLook; the look is Unity-side (each SolitonTunnelConfigSO's Look / Spindle Bridge / Domain Tint, Docs/Shaders/WORMHOLE_SHADERS.md section 14). 2026-10-29 (Yash: Soliton Tunnels, an environmental fundamental): the tube's own numbers moved off MeerkatSolitonConfig onto the two SolitonTunnelConfigSO assets in Assets/_SO_Assets/Environment/SolitonTunnel/ - SolitonTunnel.asset (RT's single tunnel: bendRadius, throat/mouthDiameter, oval*, form/stay/collapseSeconds, bridge*, rideSpeedTunnelScale) and SolitonNetwork.asset (the omnicrystal's: the page's labyrinth* keys become network*, rootTip / rootGnarl become networkTip / networkGnarl); rideExitMultiplier (exitMultiplier) and rootBounce (bounce) set both; rootMaxSpeed sets the network's maxSpeed (the single tunnel's is Unity-side). The ride is now a slip-and-slide (radial wall gravity, a small RT push, no stick), so the page's rootCruise, rootThrust, rootMove, rootDrag and rootGravity are retired: wallGravity, thrust, minSpeed and wallFriction are Unity-side.",
